&lt;p&gt;You are warmly invited to attend the first Fall 2026 session of the Dean&amp;rsquo;s Distinguished Lecture Series,&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Building Bridges for Oral Health Research&lt;/em&gt;, on&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Thursday, September 17, 2026, from 12:00&amp;ndash;1:00 PM&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;in the Hammer Health Sciences Center, HSC 3rd Floor, Room 301.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are honored to welcome Marko Vujicic, PhD,&amp;nbsp;Chief Economist &amp;amp; Vice President of the Health Policy Institute, and Chief of International Relations at the American Dental Association.&amp;nbsp;His lecture, &amp;ldquo;Evidence-Based Policy Making in Oral Health: What Research is Missing?&amp;rdquo; will take a macro‑level view of progress in oral health in the United States, including areas where progress remains limited, while outlining key policy reforms to accelerate improvement and identifying the knowledge gaps and research needed to address them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This monthly seminar series will foster collaboration and engage students in research initiatives. Faculty, staff, researchers, students, and residents are encouraged to attend and participate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Participants are eligible for 1 CE credit&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lunch will be provided for pre-registered attendees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We look forward to your participation in this exciting addition to our academic community!&lt;/p&gt;
