&lt;p&gt;Join the Human Rights Institute (HRI) for the launch of this new book, which examines the uneven power dynamics in transnational human rights advocacy and explores how organizations are working to shift power and reshape practice toward decolonial solidarity. The authors, which include Prof. Sarah Knuckey, Faculty Director of HRI, will discuss the book&amp;#39;s key arguments and takeaways from years of advocacy research, followed by Q&amp;amp;A and an HRI annual welcome reception.&lt;/p&gt;
