&lt;p&gt;This fall, join CTL Executive Director and &lt;a href="https://ctl.columbia.edu/resources-and-technology/resources/podcast/"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Dead Ideas in Teaching and Learning&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; podcast host, Amanda Irvin, to explore how some Dead Ideas--ideas that persist despite being untrue or no longer serving us (Pike 2011)-- might resurface as we reckon with AI&amp;rsquo;s impact on teaching and learning in higher education. There are two opportunities to join these lunchtime conversations on &amp;ldquo;zombie ideas&amp;rdquo; in the Fall 2026 semester: &lt;a href="https://events.columbia.edu/cal/event/eventView.do?calPath=%2Fpublic%2Fcals%2FMainCal&amp;amp;guid=CAL-00bbdb7c-9e687fb8-019e-698c4e03-00001fc3events@columbia.edu&amp;amp;recurrenceId=" target="_blank"&gt;September 18&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://events.columbia.edu/cal/event/eventView.do?calPath=%2Fpublic%2Fcals%2FMainCal&amp;amp;guid=CAL-00bbdb7c-9e687fb8-019e-6995382b-00002108events@columbia.edu&amp;amp;recurrenceId=" target="_blank"&gt;October 22&lt;/a&gt;. Please register for each separately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the first of these two conversations, we will take a deep dive into questions about who is &amp;ldquo;responsible&amp;rdquo; for AI output. Our conversation will use two podcast episodes as a springboard: &amp;ldquo;&lt;a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/2DMSaSvmTSGNUNRwh9e3Hy?si=9b-7DwFkQAiriM7lQyufzg"&gt;Redefining Academic Integrity in the Age of AI&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rdquo; with Phill Dawson, Co-Director of the Centre for Research in Assessment and Digital Learning at Deakin University and &amp;ldquo;&amp;lsquo;&lt;a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/4ePZ3JiQHHUPdf7umd9qRn?si=NWrhYk9qQX6gVZZOOHsfGQ"&gt;Constitutively Irresponsible&amp;rsquo;: Why Students Can&amp;rsquo;t be GenAI&amp;rsquo;s Quality Control&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rdquo; with Gene Flenady, Lecturer in Philosophy at Monash University, and Robert Sparrow, Professor of Philosophy at Monash University. Please listen to these podcast episodes, as you&amp;rsquo;re able, before the conversation. You can find the &lt;em&gt;Dead Ideas &lt;/em&gt;podcast on Spotify, Apple Podcasts, or streaming on the CTL website.&lt;/p&gt;
