&lt;p&gt;This month&amp;rsquo;s seminar hosted by the Center for Sexual and Gender Minority Health Research at Columbia University School of Nursing will feature LaRon E. Nelson, PhD, RN, FNP, FNAP, FNYAM, FAAN, Independence Foundation Professor of Nursing at Yale University School of Nursing. The title of his talk is &amp;ldquo;Leveraging Commercial Determinants to Advance Sexual and Gender Minority Health.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dr. Nelson&amp;rsquo;s research focuses on implementation science and multi-level interventions to reduce race- and sexuality-based disparities in HIV outcomes, with particular attention to Black men who have sex with men and African, Caribbean, and Black communities. His presentation will explore how commercial determinants can be leveraged to advance sexual and gender minority health and inform more equitable approaches to research, practice, and public health intervention.&lt;/p&gt;
