&lt;p&gt;The eminent Hungarian composer Gy&amp;ouml;rgy Kurt&amp;aacute;g celebrates his 100th birthday this year. Renowned for works built from strikingly brief movements, Kurt&amp;aacute;g distills profound emotion into the fewest possible notes, creating a listening experience of remarkable intimacy. To mark this milestone, three distinguished interpreters of his music&amp;mdash;soprano Tony Arnold, violinist Christopher Otto, and pianist Amy Williams&amp;mdash;come together for a rare performance of seldom-heard works.&lt;/p&gt;
